==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʌɡ/}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|ugge|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{term|uggr||fear, apprehension, dread|lang=non}}, related to {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|ógn||terror, threat, dispute|lang=non}} and {{term|agi||terror, strife, fear, punishment|lang=non}}. More at {{l|en|awe}}.

====Alternative forms====
* [[ugg]]

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} [[fear|Fear]]; [[horror]].
# {{context|dialectal|lang=en}} A [[surfeit]].

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|ugly}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|uggen|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{term|ugga||to fear|lang=non}}, see above.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|ugg}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|ugg|ed}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} To [[feel]] [[dread]], [[loathing]] or [[disgust]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} To fear, feel [[horror]]; [[shudder]] with horror.

====References====
* {{R:Century 1914}}

===Etymology 3===
Derived from the similarity between the letter [[u]] and the Greek letter [[µ]].

